WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.815 --> 00:00:02.061
- [Narrator] Pubs.

00:00:02.061 --> 00:00:03.775
(lively music)

00:00:03.775 --> 00:00:05.098
There's thousands of them,

00:00:05.098 --> 00:00:07.297
but this story is about just four.

00:00:07.297 --> 00:00:09.074
And what makes them so special?

00:00:09.074 --> 00:00:10.764
They're old.

00:00:10.764 --> 00:00:12.616
This guys thinks his pub is oldest.

00:00:12.616 --> 00:00:14.766
- I'm a fair bit older, all right.

00:00:14.766 --> 00:00:16.161
- Nah.
- No way.

00:00:16.161 --> 00:00:17.996
- [Narrator] I guess we
should look into this.

00:00:17.996 --> 00:00:19.893
In that case, welcome to the search

00:00:19.893 --> 00:00:21.631
for the oldest pub in the world.

00:00:21.631 --> 00:00:23.331
Take the floor, landlord one.

00:00:23.331 --> 00:00:25.143
- Welcome to Ye Olde Trip to Jerusalem,

00:00:25.143 --> 00:00:26.884
the oldest pub in England.

00:00:26.884 --> 00:00:29.401
So the landlord boards go back to 1760,

00:00:29.401 --> 00:00:31.354
but we know the caves go back to 1070

00:00:31.354 --> 00:00:33.093
when the first castle was built.

00:00:33.093 --> 00:00:34.627
Up here.

00:00:34.627 --> 00:00:36.587
Here is the wooden galleon.

00:00:36.587 --> 00:00:38.386
Don't touch it though!

00:00:38.386 --> 00:00:41.950
Everyone who's cleaned it
has come to a mysterious end.

00:00:41.950 --> 00:00:44.077
Who knows if we're the
oldest pub in the world,

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:48.116
but we sure serve the
best pint in the world.

00:00:48.116 --> 00:00:49.850
- [Narrator] Landlord two, you're up.

00:00:49.850 --> 00:00:51.118
- Welcome to the Old Ferry Boat,

00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:53.518
the oldest pub in England,
and possibly the world.

00:00:53.518 --> 00:00:54.884
- [Narrator] Isn't that
what the last guy said?

00:00:54.884 --> 00:00:56.219
- No, no, no, it is.

00:00:56.219 --> 00:00:57.462
- [Narrator] Fine.

00:00:57.462 --> 00:00:59.472
- This pub has been
dated back to 1050 a.d.

00:00:59.472 --> 00:01:01.782
But legend has it, it's 500 years older.

00:01:01.782 --> 00:01:04.092
So it's pretty old, pretty damn old.

00:01:04.092 --> 00:01:05.574
We don't have any silly ships here

00:01:05.574 --> 00:01:06.967
but we do have a ghost.

00:01:06.967 --> 00:01:08.613
This pub was built on the grave of

00:01:08.613 --> 00:01:10.660
a young girl called Juliet.

00:01:10.660 --> 00:01:13.451
But one thing's for sure:
we do serve the best pint.

00:01:13.451 --> 00:01:14.936
- [Narrator] Let's hear it landlord three.

00:01:14.936 --> 00:01:16.590
- Welcome to Ye Olde Man and Scythe.

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:18.092
It's so old, we don't even know

00:01:18.092 --> 00:01:19.743
exactly how old it is.

00:01:19.743 --> 00:01:21.792
The records go back to 1251,

00:01:21.792 --> 00:01:23.274
but the design of our cellar

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:24.689
is before the turn of the century.

00:01:24.689 --> 00:01:26.241
- [Narrator] So, you don't know.

00:01:26.241 --> 00:01:28.480
- Definitely older than
the others, though.

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.313
- [Narrator] Right.

00:01:29.313 --> 00:01:31.256
- One ghost? We've got way more than that.

00:01:31.256 --> 00:01:33.536
We've got 53, and one in particular

00:01:33.536 --> 00:01:35.393
is way better than their’s.

00:01:35.393 --> 00:01:39.029
In 1651, James Stanley,
the seventh Earl of Derby,

00:01:39.029 --> 00:01:41.014
was executed right here during the

00:01:41.014 --> 00:01:42.315
English Civil War.

00:01:42.315 --> 00:01:45.876
Head (cutting noise).

00:01:45.876 --> 00:01:48.359
Oldest pub in the world? We think so.

00:01:48.359 --> 00:01:49.773
But one thing's for sure,

00:01:49.773 --> 00:01:51.697
we pull the best pint in the world.

00:01:51.697 --> 00:01:52.943
- [Narrator] Wait, I haven't introduced--

00:01:52.943 --> 00:01:54.117
- I'll stop you there.

00:01:54.117 --> 00:01:55.503
There are many who claim to be the oldest.

00:01:55.503 --> 00:01:56.738
Well, we are fully researched,

00:01:56.738 --> 00:01:58.545
and dated as the oldest.

00:01:58.545 --> 00:01:59.462
Come on in.

00:02:00.629 --> 00:02:02.254
You're very welcome to Sean's.

00:02:02.254 --> 00:02:03.669
The bar itself is actually older

00:02:03.669 --> 00:02:04.906
than the town itself.

00:02:04.906 --> 00:02:07.184
Almost all of the owners are on record,

00:02:07.184 --> 00:02:10.457
even back to the original
owner Lou himself in 900.

00:02:10.457 --> 00:02:12.637
And he'd drive people across the Old Ford.

00:02:12.637 --> 00:02:13.470
Just here.

00:02:14.454 --> 00:02:16.994
Over here on the walls
is a letter and cert

00:02:16.994 --> 00:02:18.692
from the Guinness Book of World Records.

00:02:18.692 --> 00:02:19.876
- [Narrator] Have we found it?

00:02:19.876 --> 00:02:22.163
- You have found it, and
you're very welcome to Sean's.

00:02:22.163 --> 00:02:23.591
Every bar is going to claim to have

00:02:23.591 --> 00:02:25.130
the best beer in the world, but we can

00:02:25.130 --> 00:02:27.316
certainly claim we have the
best whiskey in the world.

00:02:27.316 --> 00:02:28.362
(glasses clinking)

00:02:28.362 --> 00:02:29.695
- [Narrator] This has
got to be the best excuse

00:02:29.695 --> 00:02:31.445
for a pub crawl ever.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:36.686
Cheers!
(lively music)

